@*
    The only route by which uBookIt emits its own styling.

    A consuming site opts in with one line in the head of its layout, rendering
    this partial by its path: ~/Views/Shared/UBookIt/_Styles.cshtml

    Three reasons it is a partial rather than a link element the site writes itself.

    Head placement. The flows render from ViewComponents, and a ViewComponent
    cannot contribute to the document head — a Razor section does not cross that
    boundary, the same boundary that makes ModelState unavailable to the flow and
    forced the TempData workaround. So a stylesheet emitted from inside a flow
    could only ever be a link in the body, which buys a flash of unstyled content
    on the very surface that has no JavaScript to hide it.

    Cascade order. The package's defaults must come before the site's overrides,
    and that ordering is a property of where this partial sits rather than
    something a token can express. Sites are documented to link their own
    stylesheet after this one.

    A theme's off-switch. A future theme replaces what this partial emits and turns
    the package's CSS off without the consuming site changing anything. That is why
    the requirement is that this be the ONLY emission route: a second link element
    somewhere else would survive the theme and fight it.

    Note for anyone editing this file: Razor comments do NOT nest. An inner comment
    closes this one early and everything below becomes live markup, which is how the
    first version of this file failed to compile.
*@
<link rel="stylesheet" href="~/_content/UBookIt.Web/ubookit.css" />
